{"step_index":4186,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T23:00:34Z","thinking":"Observed a discrepancy in Review #3 for Cure Pharma. The requested medication, \"باروفين 30 قرص\", differs in pack size from the offered \"باروفين ٢٠ قرص\", despite the name being identical. The system correctly flagged \"باروفين\" for review, achieving 100% accuracy.\n\n\nIdentified a potential OCR error in the El-Salam Shebeen catalog where \"ميمو\" (Memo) by Julphar might be a scan of \"ميبو\" (Mebo), a known Julphar product. Verified that Julphar manufactures Mebo in Egypt. Concluded that the entry should be corrected to \"ميبو مرهم صغير/جلفار\".\n\n\nThe system correctly identified several matches. However, the last entry presents a potential error: \"نيوكاربون\" (New Carbon) is being matched to \"اوكاربون\" (Eucar). This requires verification as they are distinct medications. The database must be checked to confirm if \"نيوكاربون\" is indeed a correct entry, or if \"اوكاربون\" is the intended match.\n\n\nConfirmed \"نيوكاربون\" and \"اوكاربون\" are distinct brands, requiring separate entries. Verified Topging Advance and Ketolac matches. Noticed a potential medication name error: \"هيدروكين\" versus \"هيدروكينينا\", which could represent different drugs, requiring clarification.\n\nExamined the first six entries in Cure Pharma. Noted several correct matches. Encountered another potential discrepancy: The final entry, involving a medication name, needs further scrutiny.\n\n\nA potential OCR error exists between \"Aripiprex\" and \"Ribopax\"; \"Ribopax\" requires verification. Confirmed \"Protoloc\" and \"Controloc\" are different brands of the same active ingredient.\n\nIdentified several correct matches. Note discrepancies between \"Benox\" and \"Benoxa\", and \"Panthenol El-Nile\" and \"Panthenol Urox\", requiring further investigation to ensure accuracy.\n\n\nVerified several correct matches, except for one entry where the quantities of tablets differed significantly between the input and output, which requires further investigation. Identified further correct matches in المكرومي المنصورة catalog.\n\n\nConfirmed the initial seven entries in the new data source are correct. Noted a potential discrepancy in one entry related to drug names; Grantril (إيفا) versus Grantil (ماركيرل) requires verification. The final entry from the initial group is correct.\n\nObserved all seven matches for the specified pharmacy are correct.\n\n\nIdentified several correct matches, focusing on the El-Hadaba data. Found a key discrepancy: \"سكينورين\" (Skinoren) is mismatched with \"سكينوريتش\" (Skinorich), different brands. Noted several potential OCR errors: \"اليرزون\" with \"البزون\", \"يوكيراتو\" with \"یوریکیر\". Some entries required verification.\n\n\nObserved that several new matches were identified. The increase in matches, from 72 to 93, is attributed to added preprocessing steps which included Persian/Urdu OCR normalization and punctuation removal, and the addition of common terms to stopword lists. Suspect that these preprocessing changes improved candidate retrieval for ambiguous items. Noted a critical distinction needing verification: \"Sinopril Co\" versus \"Sinopril 2 mg\" require differentiation based on the \"Co\" suffix's indication of a combination drug.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"import sys\nsys.path.insert(0, '.')\nimport openpyxl\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom rapidfuzz import fuzz\nfrom src.extract.excel_reader import read_excel, extract_item_names\nfrom src.extract.pdf_reader import parse_structured_result\nfrom src.fast_match.search import extract_brand_tokens, extract_form_group, normalize_for_search\n\nresults_path = Path(\"data/processes/PROC-001/results_PROC-001.xlsx\")\nwb = openpyxl.load_workbook(results_path, data_only=True)\n\n# 1. Collect all matched and review items from the latest results\nmatched_reqs = set()\nreview_reqs = set()\n\nfor sheetname in wb.sheetnames:\n    ws = wb[sheetname]\n    if \"ملخص\" in sheetname:\n        continue\n    if \"يحتاج مراجعة\" in sheetname:\n        for row in list(ws.iter_rows(values_only=True))[1:]:\n            if row and len(row) > 1 and row[1]:\n                review_reqs.add(str(row[1]).strip())\n    elif \"لم يُعثر عليه\" in sheetname:\n        continue\n    else:\n        for row in list(ws.iter_rows(values_only=True))[1:]:\n            if row and row[0]:\n                matched_reqs.add(str(row[0]).strip())\n\nprint(f\"Total matched items: {len(matched_reqs)}\")\nprint(f\"Total review items: {len(review_reqs)}\")\n\n# 2. Shortages\nshortages_file = Path(\"data/processes/PROC-001/input_shortages/0913.xlsx\")\nshortage_rows = read_excel(shortages_file)\nshortage_items = extract_item_names(shortage_rows, name_column=\"أسم الصنف\")\nall_shortages = list({item[\"item_name_raw\"].strip() for item in shortage_items if item[\"item_name_raw\"]})\n\nunmatched = [s for s in all_shortages if s not in matched_reqs and s not in review_reqs]\nprint(f\"Total unique unmatched shortages: {len(unmatched)}\")\n\n# 3. Warehouses\nwh_dir = Path(\"data/processes/PROC-001/input_warehouses\")\ncache_dir = Path(\"data/processes/data/.unstructured_cache\")\n\nwarehouses_data = {}\nfor pdf_file in wh_dir.glob(\"*.pdf\"):\n    alongside = pdf_file.with_suffix('.json')\n    items = []\n    if alongside.exists():\n        with open(alongside, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n            data = json.load(f)\n        items = parse_structured_result(data, pdf_file.name)\n    else:\n        import hashlib\n        hasher = hashlib.md5()\n        with open(pdf_file, 'rb') as f:\n            buf = f.read(65536)\n            while len(buf) > 0:\n                hasher.update(buf)\n                buf = f.read(65536)\n        h = hasher.hexdigest()\n        cache_file = cache_dir / f\"{h}_extract.json\"\n        if cache_file.exists():\n            with open(cache_file, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n                data = json.load(f)\n            items = parse_structured_result(data, pdf_file.name)\n    wh_names = [it[\"item_name_raw\"].strip() for it in items if it.get(\"item_name_raw\")]\n    warehouses_data[pdf_file.stem] = wh_names\n\n# 4. Deep False Negative Check for the remaining 498 items\nmisses = []\nfor s in unmatched:\n    s_norm = normalize_for_search(s)\n    s_brand = extract_brand_tokens(s)\n    s_form = extract_form_group(s)\n    \n    for wh_name, items in warehouses_data.items():\n        for w in items:\n            w_norm = normalize_for_search(w)\n            w_brand = extract_brand_tokens(w)\n            w_form = extract_form_group(w)\n            \n            # Form check\n            if s_form and w_form and s_form != w_form:\n                continue\n                \n            # Exact brand token match or high ratio\n            b_ratio = fuzz.ratio(s_brand, w_brand)\n            ts_ratio = fuzz.token_sort_ratio(s, w)\n            \n            if s_brand and w_brand and (s_brand == w_brand or (b_ratio >= 80 and len(s_brand) >= 4)):\n                misses.append({\n                    \"shortage\": s,\n                    \"warehouse\": wh_name,\n                    \"wh_item\": w,\n                    \"b_ratio\": b_ratio,\n                    \"ts_ratio\": ts_ratio,\n                    \"s_form\": s_form,\n                    \"w_form\": w_form\n                })\n\nmisses.sort(key=lambda x: x[\"ts_ratio\"], reverse=True)\nprint(f\"\\nRemaining candidate matches among 'Not Found': {len(misses)}\")\nseen = set()\nfor m in misses:\n    k = (m['shortage'], m['wh_item'])\n    if k not in seen:\n        seen.add(k)\n        print(f\"[{m['warehouse']}]\")\n        print(f\"  Req: '{m['shortage']}'\")\n        print(f\"  Wh : '{m['wh_item']}'\")\n        print(f\"  Score: ts={m['ts_ratio']} | b_ratio={m['b_ratio']} | form={m['s_form']} vs {m['w_form']}\\n\")\n","Description":"Deep scan of the remaining unmatched items","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\scratch\\scan_remaining_unmatched.py","toolAction":"Write script","toolSummary":"Scan remaining unmatched items"}}]}
